From 8c98bff3a85d203f23d7b29471a32b4840217c29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Farhan <farhanabdm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:34:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gi): import custom character packs

Add "Import Characters (.json)" to the Custom Characters dialog. It reads
packs made by tools/custom-characters/nanoka-to-go.mjs and adds each
character as an imported custom character; a character imported before
(same source id) is updated.

Imported characters keep their own level curves, ascension stats and
per-level talent multipliers. Their sheet is built from the talent rows:
Normal Attack rows and rows named "... DMG" become damage formulas, other
rows are shown as values, and constellations that raise a talent level
are applied. Images come from an existing character of the same element
and weapon type. A new editor changes their base stats at level 90 and
every talent multiplier per level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Asb8vZRqeTYT9zLpVizGNv
